  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-04-13T23:50:38.835Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "# Issue:\n\nInvite Photos are now also being taken with the normal camera, which is great! \n\nThere are a few issues with how this is currently implemented though.\n\n1. The Camera does not tell you anywhere that you are taking an Invite Photo\n\n2. You can easily swap out of taking an invite Photo without ever noticing it\n\n# Suggestion:  \n\nThe Camera should be out into some sort of \"Invite Mode\" when taking pictures for an Invite / Invite Request\n\nThis mode should do 2 things:\n\n1. Tell the user that they are currently taking an Invite / Invite Request Photo with some sort of banner\n\n2. Prevent the user from changing the Camera Mode \n\nThere should probably also be some sort of button to Exit this mode, so that if the user decides that they don't want to take an Invite Photo any more and just want to use the camera normally again they can.\n\n# Attachments:  \n\nHere is a video showcasing the issue:\n\nhttps://streamable.com/9ker8l",
